content:
An unread email earns a place in the briefing when at least one holds:
- it asks the user a direct question or for a decision;
- it is from someone the user meets today;
- it blocks someone else's work until answered;
- it concerns anything named in the installation's 'focus' setting;
- it carries a deadline inside the next two working days.

Newsletters, notifications, receipts, CC-only threads with no question, and anything the user already answered from another device do not qualify. When more than seven items qualify, keep the seven most consequential and say how many were left out. Judgement over rules: a two-line email from the CEO matters; a 2,000-word update addressed to forty people usually does not.
